---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Chauncy - Search by Meaning. Local-First. For Readers, Writers, and Researchers." description="Chauncy is a local-first tool for the writing, research, and reading you want to keep working with. Search by meaning across PDFs, email, notes, and web pages. Your files stay on your machine.">

  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A local-first tool for readers, writers, and researchers</p>
        <h1>For people who remember the point, not the filename.</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          Chauncy is a local-first tool for the writing, research, and reading you want to keep working with. Bring in the documents you already have, add new material as you find it, and search by meaning across all of it.
        </p>
        <p class="hero-body">
          Ask in plain English. Inspect the source. Follow the connections.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-primary">Buy Chauncy for Windows - $99</a>
          <a href="#how-it-works" class="btn btn-secondary">See how it works</a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-trust">
          <span>No account</span>
          <span>Your files stay local</span>
          <span>No tracking</span>
          <span>No autonomous actions</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="product-mockup" aria-label="Chauncy semantic search preview">
        <div class="mock-nav">
          <span class="mock-tab active">Workspace</span>
          <span class="mock-tab">Add</span>
          <span class="mock-tab">Settings</span>
          <span class="mock-status">Engine ready</span>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-caption mock-caption-top">Chauncy surfaces evidence. You do the thinking.</div>
        <div class="mock-body">
          <div class="mock-results">
            <div class="mock-search">
              <p class="mock-query-label">Search input</p>
              <div class="mock-query">natural camouflage</div>
              <div class="mock-card selected">
                <div>
                  <strong>How Zebra Stripes Confuse Predators</strong>
                  <p>The high-contrast pattern disrupts motion detection in biting flies and disorients group predators when zebras gather in herds.</p>
                  <p class="mock-callout">The word "camouflage" does not appear in this article.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="mock-search">
              <p class="mock-query-label">Search input</p>
              <div class="mock-query">advice about handling difficult conversations</div>
              <div class="mock-card">
                <div>
                  <strong>Email from Dan, 2018-03-14</strong>
                  <p>...the trick isn't winning the argument. It's making sure they walk out still wanting to talk to you next month...</p>
                  <p class="mock-callout">No words in common with the query. Chauncy matched the topic.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="mock-panel">
            <p class="mock-panel-label">Connected material</p>
            <h3>Chauncy surfaces evidence. You do the thinking.</h3>
            <p>Open a source, compare related material, add your interpretation, and keep the trail attached to the documents.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="mock-caption mock-caption-bottom">Open a source, compare related material, add your interpretation, and keep the trail attached to the documents.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container screenshot-section">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">The real product</p>
        <h2>Windows workspace, ready to search.</h2>
        <p>Chauncy runs as a desktop app on your machine. Here is the workspace after material is in the library.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="product-shot">
        <img src="/images/chauncy-workspace.png" alt="Chauncy desktop workspace showing search and document results" width="1732" height="987" loading="lazy" />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="who-for" class="section-alt">
    <div class="container who-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Fit check</p>
        <h2>Who Chauncy is for — and who it is not.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="who-cards">
        <div class="who-card yes">
          <h3>Built for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Researchers, writers, consultants, and analysts with large personal archives</li>
            <li>People who remember the point of a document, not the filename</li>
            <li>Anyone who wants meaning-based search without building a knowledge graph by hand</li>
            <li>Users who want local-first storage and optional bring-your-own AI</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="who-card no">
          <h3>Not built for</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>HIPAA, attorney-client privilege, or other compliance-regulated environments</li>
            <li>Teams that need multi-user sharing or cloud sync today</li>
            <li>People looking for an autonomous agent that acts on their behalf</li>
            <li>Mac users at launch — join the <a href="/waitlist">waitlist</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="compare" class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it fits</p>
        <h2>Different job than notes apps, desktop search, or chatbots.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="compare-grid">
        <div class="compare-card">
          <h3>vs note / PKM tools</h3>
          <p>Obsidian-style tools ask you to tag, backlink, and maintain structure. Chauncy infers connections from meaning so the work is reading and writing, not gardening a graph.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-card">
          <h3>vs desktop search</h3>
          <p>Spotlight and Everything match keywords and filenames. Chauncy matches meaning — a query can surface a document that shares no words with your search.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="compare-card">
          <h3>vs uploading to a chatbot</h3>
          <p>Chat tools need re-upload theater and live in the cloud. Chauncy indexes a local archive once, searches offline, and only sends excerpts if you turn AI on.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="safety" class="section-alt">
    <div class="container safety-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Private and safe by architecture.</p>
        <h2>Chauncy is not a runaway agent.</h2>
        <p>
          It does not browse the web for you, operate accounts, send email, buy things, delete files, or chain together background actions. Chauncy is a tool for working with material you've chosen to keep.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="safety-cards">
        <div class="safety-card">
          <h3>Local first</h3>
          <p>Your documents, search index, embeddings, and annotations live on your machine.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="safety-card">
          <h3>Optional AI</h3>
          <p>AI synthesis is optional. You choose whether to use it, which provider, and when excerpts leave your machine.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="safety-card">
          <h3>Human judgment</h3>
          <p>Chauncy can surface connections. It does not decide what is true, important, or ready to publish.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container section-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">No system to maintain</p>
      <h2>The structure is in the meaning. You don't build it.</h2>
      <p>
        Other tools require you to do the organizing yourself — tagging, backlinking, sticking to naming conventions, keeping the system tidy for years before the connections become useful. Chauncy reads what you've already written and infers the structure itself. The work you put in is the reading and the writing. The connections follow.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="how-it-works" class="section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">Workflow</p>
        <h2>A practice that compounds.</h2>
        <p>Start with what you have. Add what you read. Chauncy becomes more useful as your collection grows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow-grid">
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>01</span>
          <h3>Curate</h3>
          <p>Decide what's worth keeping. Add PDFs, email, Markdown, Word, PowerPoint, HTML, web URLs, and notes — files already on your machine, or new material as you encounter it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>02</span>
          <h3>Ask</h3>
          <p>Use plain English to search by meaning, not just filename, folder, or exact keyword.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>03</span>
          <h3>Inspect</h3>
          <p>Open the source, check the surrounding context, and see related material beside it.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="workflow-step">
          <span>04</span>
          <h3>Interpret</h3>
          <p>Add your annotations, draw your conclusions, and keep the reasoning trail attached to the sources.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">What you can bring in</p>
        <h2>Multiple paths in. One library out.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list ingestion-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Files and folders</h3>
          <p>Point Chauncy at individual files or whole folder trees. PDFs, Word, PowerPoint, Markdown, HTML, and plain text — recursively, if you want.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Email</h3>
          <p>Forward selected messages to a dedicated folder, drop saved emails into a watch folder, or ingest directly from an IMAP mailbox you configure.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Web pages</h3>
          <p>Paste a URL and Chauncy fetches and indexes the page. A browser extension for one-click capture is in development.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Voice input</h3>
          <p>Dictate search queries and notes directly into Chauncy using your machine's voice recognition.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="section-note">Ingestion is always your choice. Chauncy doesn't scan your drive or pull from the cloud without you asking it to.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI on your terms</p>
        <h2>Search works without AI. Add AI when you want it.</h2>
        <p>Chauncy's semantic search runs locally — no AI provider needed, nothing leaving your machine. When you want AI to summarize, draft, or answer questions across your sources, turn synthesis on and connect a provider.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="provider-list">
        <span>Anthropic or OpenAI with your own API key</span>
        <span>Ollama running on your own hardware</span>
        <span>Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint you configure</span>
      </div>
      <p class="section-note">Switch providers any time. Your files stay on your machine — only the excerpt you ask about leaves, and only when you initiate the request.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="features" class="section">
    <div class="container feature-split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Capabilities</p>
        <h2>What Chauncy does.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-list">
        <div>
          <h3>Semantic retrieval</h3>
          <p>Find the memo, quote, email, or note even when you can't remember the exact words.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Automatic connections</h3>
          <p>See related material across formats and projects — no tagging, backlinking, or organizing required.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Your interpretation, kept with the source</h3>
          <p>Attach your reactions to source material — questions, connections, confirmations, conclusions. Annotations become part of the searchable collection and travel with the documents they describe.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="container cta-block">
      <p class="eyebrow">Windows installer is ready</p>
      <h2>Windows launch pricing.</h2>
      <p>One-time purchase: $99. Buy through Stripe and download the Windows installer immediately. No account required.</p>
      <a href="/pricing" class="btn btn-primary">Buy Chauncy for Windows - $99</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 6rem 0 5rem;
  }

  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.92fr) minmax(520px, 1.08fr);
    align-items: center;
    gap: 3rem;
  }

  .hero-copy h1 {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .hero-sub {
    margin-top: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .hero-body {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .hero-actions {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .hero-trust {
    margin-top: 1.35rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }

  .hero-trust span {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.6rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .product-mockup {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-bright);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: #050505;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .mock-nav {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1.15rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.76);
  }

  .mock-tab {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mock-tab.active {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .mock-status {
    margin-left: auto;
    color: var(--color-success);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mock-caption {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .mock-caption-top {
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem 0;
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mock-caption-bottom {
    padding: 0 1.2rem 1.2rem;
  }

  .mock-body {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.35fr 0.9fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.2rem;
  }

  .mock-results {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .mock-search,
  .mock-panel {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: var(--color-bg-secondary);
  }

  .mock-search {
    padding: 0.85rem;
  }

  .mock-query-label {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .mock-query {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.75rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-bright);
    border-radius: 10px;
    color: var(--color-text);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
    font-size: 0.86rem;
  }

  .mock-card {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 0.7rem;
    padding: 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.28);
  }

  .mock-card.selected {
    border-color: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.48);
    background: rgba(14, 165, 233, 0.08);
  }

  .mock-card strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .mock-card p,
  .mock-panel p {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .mock-card span {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mock-callout {
    color: var(--color-primary-hover) !important;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mock-panel {
    padding: 1rem;
    align-self: stretch;
  }

  .mock-panel-label {
    color: var(--color-primary) !important;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .safety-grid,
  .feature-split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .safety-grid p,
  .section-copy p,
  .section-intro p,
  .section-note,
  .cta-block p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .section-copy {
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .safety-cards,
  .feature-list,
  .workflow-grid,
  .provider-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.7rem;
  }

  .provider-list span {
    padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .mode-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .safety-cards {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }

  .safety-card,
  .workflow-step,
  .feature-list > div,
  .mode-card {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .safety-card p,
  .workflow-step p,
  .feature-list p,
  .mode-card p {
    margin-top: 0.55rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .section-intro {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .workflow-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  }

  .workflow-step span {
    color: var(--color-primary);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 750;
  }

  .workflow-step h3 {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }

  .feature-list {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .feature-list > div:last-child:nth-child(odd) {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .ingestion-list > div:last-child:nth-child(even) {
    grid-column: auto;
  }

  .mode-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }

  .section-note {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .cta-block {
    max-width: 720px;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .cta-block .btn {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .screenshot-section .section-intro {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .product-shot {
    margin: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border-bright);
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
    background: #050505;
  }

  .product-shot img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .who-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  .who-cards,
  .compare-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .compare-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
  }

  .who-card,
  .compare-card {
    padding: 1.35rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  .who-card h3,
  .compare-card h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .who-card ul {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.65rem;
  }

  .who-card li,
  .compare-card p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .who-card.yes li::before {
    content: '✓ ';
    color: var(--color-success);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .who-card.no li::before {
    content: '× ';
    color: var(--color-warning);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .hero-grid,
    .safety-grid,
    .feature-split,
    .who-cards,
    .compare-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .product-mockup {
      max-width: 760px;
    }

    .workflow-grid,
    .safety-cards,
    .mode-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .hero {
      padding-top: 4rem;
    }

    .mock-body,
    .workflow-grid,
    .safety-cards,
    .feature-list,
    .mode-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .feature-list > div:last-child:nth-child(odd) {
      grid-column: auto;
    }

    .product-mockup {
      display: none;
    }
  }
</style>
